- Guest series outcome: `passed`; both runs loaded Linux, emitted their generated unique nonce exactly once, and reached `budget_exhausted` at `retired=2,999,999,998`.
- Strict automatic comparison: `matches=false`, process exit code 1. Explained fields are run ID/nonce, raw runner JSON hash, UART hash/path and wall time. Unexplained fields are `machine_observations` and `ordered_uart_bytes` after the existing nonce/Stage 4 normalization.
- The Stage 4 nonce eligibility gate was false for this pair because the terminal panic snapshots contain unallowlisted optional frames (run 0001 includes `? common_interrupt`; run 0002 includes `? console_srcu_read_unlock` and `? tty_ldisc_deref`). Therefore the comparator did not apply the Stage 4 volatile-field projection. It compared the complete stop record after removing only `com1_hex`, `com1_text`, and `machine_stop_reason` and normalizing nonce strings; 29 raw machine leaf paths differ: `cr3`, `cr3_changes`, 11 `gpr` leaves, `halt_idle_ns`, `irq0_edges`, `irq_refused_masked`, `irq_refused_shadow`, `irqs_delivered`, two `last_cr3_change` leaves, `quanta`, `quantum_cut_by_deadline`, `rdtsc_reads`, `rdtsc_reads_by_cpl[0]`, `rflags`, `rip`, `rip_bytes`, `rip_gpa`, and `virtual_ns`. Delivered #PF (33/33) and #GP (1/1) match. If the existing volatile projection were hypothetically applied, its residual would be `cr3_changes`, `rdtsc_reads`, and `rdtsc_reads_by_cpl[0]`; that is not the actual comparator result for this pair. No new field was excluded.
- RDTSC count delta: 19,543 reads. This series did not request per-event execution sidecars, so it does not localize the delta to a guest RIP or capture returned TSC values.
- UART differs after nonce normalization; full UART captures are in the run directories below. No comparator normalizer was changed.

## Interpretation

This current CPU0 ACPI fixture also fails the strict unique-nonce N=2 comparator, so the old ACPI blob in earlier S5-07 runs is not the only condition under which variation occurs. A same-nonce direct replay on this current fixture was byte-identical, but that pair used an opt-in sidecar and is only a control. The current N=2 difference is consistent with guest execution depending on nonce/cmdline content or another run-state source; it does not establish causality. S5-07 remains blocked/unaccepted until strict-clean unique-nonce evidence and an explanation of the surviving RDTSC/CR3 and UART differences. No comparator rules changed.

Raw series, per-run manifests/runner JSON and complete UART files are retained locally under `work/stage5/stage5-s5-07-current-acpi-n2-20261116-a/`.
